// The field event layer's finders and helpers (k_event.c; docs/ANALYSIS/26_field.md sections 5 and 7.1), from
// SLUS_216.21. Phase 5 slice `field3`, part `event`: generated by p3fes_handgen (one statement per instruction on the
// hg_cpu register view: frame, spills, $ra links, cycle charges and check points exactly as the recompiled bodies) and
// made readable on top -- block roles, named offsets, comments; no statement moved. tests/game/test_field3_event.cpp
// pairs each body with its __recomp body.
//
// What is here:
//   * the field-of-view test sub_1C6200 (heading of a model's "at" axis against the heading towards a point, both in
//     degrees 0..360 from acosf against +z) and the "who is near / who can I see" finders built on it, on the
//     distance helper sub_4C6AC0 (|v|) and the collision ray sub_1ACC30 (line of sight, 1 = blocked):
//       - sub_1C6450: can a model see a point (FOV, distance, both rays clear);
//       - sub_1C6720 / sub_1C6A20: the nearest live unit of the hero's 4 x 4-cell bucket in range (and FOV) with a
//         clear line of sight (random floors use the bucket of the unit's own cell, other fields bucket 0);
//       - sub_1C6DD0 / sub_1C6D70 / sub_1C6F50: the nearest living party member (index / unit / in FOV);
//       - sub_1C7160 / sub_1C71F0: two units / points within a distance;
//       - sub_1C7270: the first unopened treasure box of the bucket in range;
//       - sub_1C74C0: the NPC (type-3 scene resource) the hero faces within 200 units (look-at + head turn);
//       - sub_1C7CE0: is the party member with a given DatUnit id within 1600 units of the hero;
//   * the battle hand-off: sub_1C7830 fills the 52-byte battle packet's party part (26_field.md 7.1: near members
//     join, members 2000+ units away are listed apart) and sub_1C8120 puts the far members that joined back next to
//     the hero on random floors after the battle;
//   * the exit table's free sub_1C80C0, the "field event" / "draw command" task creation and their destroy callbacks,
//     and the k_unit.c record reset sub_1CD7A0.
//
// The bucket table 0x86B180: 4 x 4 buckets of 49 words (196 bytes), bucket (bx, bz) at + 4 * (49 bx + 196 bz) where
// b = cell / 4 and cell = (int)((pos + 400) / 800) (the 800-unit grid, 26_field.md 6.2): words 0..23 = the field units
// in the bucket (null-terminated), words 24.. = the treasure boxes (null-terminated; 0x86B1E0 = word 24 of bucket 0).
